      "review_notes": "The canonical law conditions independent odds-matched binomials on the requested total; its standard product-coefficient PMF, positive normalizer, support and endpoint laws were independently reviewed and tested in Batch012. The proposal builder samples each binomial once. A single accepted-proposal expectation inequality funds amplified retries after checking the sum. Actual zero and full-population shortcuts return the corresponding deterministic count vectors. The small private constructor helpers insert verified constants after structural binders, avoiding unnecessary closure traversal; the public theorem still checks the unchanged actual source. New independent callers frame arbitrary resources and arbitrary ENNReal continuations through the whole program, and exercise empty/full shortcuts with exact literal count-vector encoders."
    },
