      "review_notes": "Consecutive chunks partition the original categorical weighted sum. Selecting a block by its total and a label by its conditional weight cancels the block total; an all-zero block contributes zero even for infinite output credits. The single expectation identity identifies the result with the independently normalized canonical WeightedChoice law. Main CTE validates, groups and totals the data, draws a supported positive block, looks it up safely and performs the conditional categorical draw. Independent tests include a leading zero-total block, a short final block, size one and size larger than the list. Infinite credits at zero-weight labels reduce to the finite expected value8/5; generic callers retain arbitrary framed resources."
    },
