      "review_notes": "The public target is the independently normalized UniformInt law. Individual retained states follow finite-horizon continuation credits, rather than an incorrect per-state uniform output claim. Appending fair bits enumerates the doubled interval; the upper accepted block emits every target once and the lower residue remains narrower than the target. The aggregate credit bound leaves exponentially vanishing cutoff mass, so an arbitrary positive error budget removes the horizon. Main CTE is finite-horizon symbolic execution, using cutoff credit1 to derive contradiction, plus one initial uniform-credit bound. Independent callers cover non-power-of-two targets3 and5, arbitrary ENNReal continuations and resources, and the singleton without UniformInt. Shared tests distinguish lower and upper orientation states with infinite credit and check exact cutoff tails."
    }
